---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { PHONE, TEL_HREF, STEPS } from '../data/site';
import { serviceSchema } from '../data/schema';

const title = 'Mobile European Auto Repair Services | Eway Auto Repairs';
const description = `European auto repair at your driveway in South Jersey: diagnostics, scheduled maintenance, brakes, coding, second opinions and pre-purchase inspections. 30+ years, ASE Master certified. Call ${PHONE}.`;

const schemas = [
  serviceSchema(
    'Mobile European Auto Repair',
    'Mobile diagnostics, maintenance, and repair for European cars in South Jersey.',
    '/services'
  ),
];

const detailed = [
  {
    anchor: 'svc-diagnostics',
    num: '01',
    title: 'Diagnostics',
    paras: [
      'Check engine lights, intermittent faults, electrical problems, and the cars another shop already gave up on. I run factory-level scan capability: full module access, live data, guided tests. A parts store code reader tells you a circuit complained and nothing past that.',
      "A code is where the diagnosis starts. It points at the circuit that reported a problem, which is rarely the same thing as the part that caused it. Thirty years on these platforms is what fills in that gap, and it's why I end up fixing cars that have already had parts thrown at them.",
    ],
  },
  {
    anchor: 'svc-maintenance',
    num: '02',
    title: 'Scheduled Maintenance',
    paras: [
      'Oil and filters, brake fluid, coolant, spark plugs, belts, transmission services. Done on the manufacturer schedule with fluids the engine is approved for. European engines are specific about oil approvals, and close enough is how they sludge up.',
      "I also do the things the maintenance display pretends don't exist. Lifetime transmission fluid, Haldex couplings, brake fluid that nobody ever flushes. The cars that make it to 200,000 miles are the ones that got those done.",
    ],
  },
  {
    anchor: 'svc-brakes',
    num: '03',
    title: 'Brakes & Suspension',
    paras: [
      'Pads, rotors, wear sensors, control arms, bushings, struts, sway bar links. Most modern European cars need the electronic parking brake retracted with a scan tool before the rear pads will come off, and the wear sensors replaced rather than bent out of the way and ignored.',
      "On suspension I'll tell you what is worn versus what turns up on a lift-and-shake inspection to fill out an estimate. Bushings crack on the outside long before they stop doing their job, and plenty of quotes don't bother with that distinction.",
    ],
  },
  {
    anchor: 'svc-coding',
    num: '04',
    title: 'Coding & Programming',
    paras: [
      'Module coding, adaptations, retrofits, and service resets that most independent shops cannot do. Battery registration on BMWs, component protection on VW and Audi, injector coding, enabling equipment the car was built with but never had switched on. The software side of a modern European car is half the work.',
      'It matters most right after a repair. A new battery, a replacement module, or a new component usually has to be introduced to the car properly. Skip that step and you inherit electrical faults that get blamed on everything else for the next two years.',
    ],
  },
  {
    anchor: 'svc-second',
    num: '05',
    title: 'Second Opinions',
    paras: [
      "Got an estimate that doesn't sit right with you? Bring it over. I'll look at the car and tell you what it needs, what can wait, and what on that sheet is padding.",
      "Usually the repair is smaller than the quote. Sometimes it isn't, and then at least you know the number is real before you spend it.",
    ],
  },
];
---

<Page title={title} description={description} path="/services" schemas={schemas}>
  <PageIntro eyebrow="Services">
    <Fragment slot="title">What I do in your <span class="accent">driveway</span>.</Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="intro">
      Diagnostics, maintenance, and repair for European cars, at your home or your workplace,
      anywhere in the South Jersey service area. Written estimate before the work, itemized
      invoice after it.
    </Fragment>
  </PageIntro>

  <section class="section-ruled">
    <div class="section container">
      {
        detailed.map((s, i) => (
          <div id={s.anchor} class:list={['svc-block']} style={i > 0 ? 'margin-top:64px' : ''}>
            <div class="eyebrow" data-reveal>{s.num}</div>
            <h2 data-reveal>{s.title}</h2>
            <div class="copy">
              {s.paras.map((p) => (
                <p>{p}</p>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        ))
      }

      <div id="ppi-overview" style="margin-top:64px">
        <div class="eyebrow" data-reveal>06</div>
        <h2 data-reveal>Pre-Purchase Inspections</h2>
        <div class="copy">
          <p>
            Buying a used European car? I inspect it where it sits, before you commit. Full
            module scan, mechanical inspection, photos, and a straight answer on whether to buy
            it. The cheapest money you will ever spend on a car.
          </p>
          <p>
            <a href="/pre-purchase-inspection">Everything that's included in an inspection</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="next-links">
        <a class="chip-link" href="/pre-purchase-inspection">Pre-Purchase Inspection</a>
        <a class="chip-link" href="/brands">Brands I work on</a>
        <a class="chip-link" href="/service-area">Service area</a>
        <a class="chip-link" href="/contact">Request a quote</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-alt">
    <div class="section container">
      <div class="eyebrow" data-reveal>How It Works</div>
      <h2 data-reveal>Four steps, no surprises.</h2>
      <div class="step-grid">
        {
          STEPS.map((st) => (
            <div class="step" data-reveal>
              <div class="numeral">{st.n}</div>
              <h3>{st.title}</h3>
              <p>{st.body}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <div class="copy" style="margin-top:44px">
        <p>
          New Jersey requires a written estimate before the work starts, written authorization
          with the odometer reading on it, and an itemized invoice that separates parts from
          labor. I worked that way before it was a rule. Call <a href={TEL_HREF}>{PHONE}</a> and
          we start with a conversation about what the car is doing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand />
</Page>
